# Level 1, played rather than walked through: rescue a victim, then go down to
# the graveyard and fight. `movies/level1.zmv` reaches gameplay and moves
# around, but no two actors in it ever touch, so the collision dispatch the
# sprite pass ends with is never reached at all (`zamn_cosim verify -c`, site
# `overlap_hit`). This one reaches it hundreds of times.
#
# CORRECTION, and the reason `movies/level1-2p.zmv` exists: the B held below
# does *nothing*. **Y is the fire button.** Not one shot is fired anywhere in
# this movie — the ammo counter reads 150 from the first frame of gameplay to
# the last — so what looks like a firefight is a man running into zombies with
# his hands full. That is why 1,226 collisions contain exactly one enemy taking
# damage. The inputs are left exactly as they were: every number in PROGRESS.md
# and docs/cosim.md was measured against these bytes, and a regression baseline
# that quietly changes cannot regress.
#
# The boot prefix through frame 1484 is level1.zmv's, unchanged: mashing Start
# through the logos, the title and the menus. Control of Zeke begins around
# frame 1830, once "LEVEL 1 / ZOMBIE PANIC" has finished loading.
#
# Retune by watching where it actually gets to:
#   zamn_headless <rom> shot.png 4200 -m movies\level1-rescue.zmv --at 1980,2500,3000
# Regenerate with tools/make_movie.sh if the timing ever needs retuning.
